course: dictionary
lesson: 13246
title: Gestation: growing before birth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are science words, and you learn them in science lessons. Gestation is one of them. When you read «Gestation lasts about three weeks for a mouse», look at the words around it. A baby is growing, and the sentence is about an animal, so gestation must be about time.
explain: Gestation means the time a baby animal grows inside its mother before it is born. Humans have a gestation of about nine months, while an elephant's is nearly two years. Use the clues to check: «The baby elephant grew inside its mother for almost two years» tells you the same idea.
explain: The word can also be used about ideas. «The plan had a long gestation before the team finally began it» means the plan took a long time to develop, like a baby growing. Swap in the meaning, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Gestation means the time a baby animal grows inside its mother before it is born.
fact: «Human gestation is about nine months.»
fact: «An elephant's gestation is nearly two years.»
fact: «A mouse's gestation is about three weeks.» Gestation can also mean the time an idea takes to develop.
exercise: «A mouse's gestation lasts about three weeks.» What does gestation mean here? | Rest time after a long run | *The time a baby grows inside its mother before birth | The time it takes to dig a hole | A type of small furry pet
exercise: «The idea had a long gestation before the team finally tried it.» What does gestation mean in this sentence? | A type of mouse | *The time an idea takes to develop | A rest after a long journey
exercise: Which animal has the longest gestation: a mouse, a human or an elephant? | Mouse | *Elephant | Human
test: «Human gestation is about nine months.» How long is human gestation? | About nine days | About nine hours | About nine years | *About nine months
test: What does gestation mean? | A sudden loud noise | A large group of animals | Something you eat for breakfast | *The time a baby grows inside its mother before it is born
exam: Mia reads «The gestation of an elephant is nearly two years» and says it means a holiday. Why is she wrong? | *Gestation means the time a baby grows inside its mother before birth | Gestation means a holiday from school | Gestation means the elephant is sleeping | Gestation means a type of food
